Open-coefficient array mode for the Fire OS 6 frontend (pmOS 8-beam profile).

--open-coefficients computes the 768-tap WOLA prototype (Kaiser-windowed sinc)
and the eight fixed beams (diffuse-field superdirective, MK2/MK3/MK5/MK6 at
their measured positions) at startup, so this frontend runs with no vendor file.
--clean-on-echo adapts the all-beam canceller only while playback is active and
passes the fixed beams through untouched otherwise. The READY banner reports
both. --merge-all outputs the mean of the eight cleaned beams. Applied by
abuild's default_prepare after the tarball is unpacked.

